Do not install libonnxruntime.so* into $out/lib.

SpeedyNote links ONNX Runtime as a private dependency. Upstream bundles the
prebuilt .so next to the binary and resolves it via INSTALL_RPATH=$ORIGIN/../lib,
which suits FHS layouts. In nixpkgs we link the nixpkgs-built onnxruntime and
resolve it from the store via RPATH; installing a copy into the output only
duplicates ~28 MB of store per closure and leaves $out/lib holding a library
that nothing else consumes.

CMake keeps the absolute path to an external library in the install RPATH
(it is no longer "installed by this project"), so removing this rule is what
makes the nix store path survive into the final binary.

Upstream-status: not submitted (packaging-specific).

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
